(“Lessor”), and the City
of Cheyenne, Wyoming
— Laramie County, State of Wyoming Joint Powers Board (“Lessee”), a
statutorily authorized entity organized and existing under the laws of the State of Wyoming,
whose address is P.O. Box 2477, Cheyenne, Wyoming 82001.
2.
Purpose of Amendment.
The purpose of this Amendment is to amend
Paragraph 6, Use of Premises, contained in the Lease agreement between the parties dated
March 9, 1992, to expressly allow, pursuant to provisions contained in Cheyenne City Code
Chapter 5.12, the sale, dispensing and consumption of alcoholic liquor and malt beverages upon
the leased premises by the Lessee or sub-lessee. Paragraph 6 of the Lease is hereby amended to
add the following language at the end of said paragraph:
“Pursuant
to provisions contained
in
Cheyenne City Code Chapter 5.12,
Alcoholic Liquor and Malt Beverages, the sale, dispensing and consumption of
alcoholic liquor and malt beverages upon the leased premises by the Lessee or
sub-lessee shall be, and hereby is, expressly allowed by the Lessee or sub-
lessee.”
3.
Other Terms and Conditions Remain Unchanged.
All other terms and
conditions of the original Lease, as amended, shall remain unchanged and in full force and
effect.
4.
Signatures.
